Ladybird resolves a gradient border image at the border-image area size,
then maps each source slice into a bounded repeated tile. The gradient
keeps its full-image geometry when a slice stretches in one or both
axes. Numeric slices scale with effective zoom; percentage slices use
the generated image dimensions. The selected image-set() option uses the
same sizing and painting path.

Blink sizes generated images in NinePieceImagePainter::Paint before
slicing them in PaintPieces. The ratio of zoomed to unzoomed image sizes
scales numeric slices into the source image coordinates.

WebKit uses BorderPainter::paintNinePieceImageImpl to size the source.
Its nine-piece painter supplies slices to Style::GradientImage::draw,
which resolves the gradient for the concrete object size before mapping
the source rectangle into its destination.

Gecko uses nsCSSBorderImageRenderer::DrawBorderImage to divide the image
into pieces. Each nsImageRenderer::DrawBorderImageComponent call gives
nsCSSGradientRenderer::Create the full image size and paints only the
source slice. Ladybird follows the same sizing and slicing behavior with
its own gradient resolver and repeated-tile records.

The reduced case and reference cases were compared with Chrome
157.0.8103.78. The reference matrix covers linear, radial, conic and
repeating gradients, transparent currentColor stops, numeric slices at
150% and 200% zoom, center fill and image-set(). The imported WPTs also
cover auto border-image widths, outsets and border radii.
